module hid-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The District of Hawaii's own periods, computed under the federal rules
// (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule"; LR1.4(d): days are calendar days).
// Most apply "unless otherwise ordered" where the rule says so. Rules that
// state no period or limit stay out, as do these: the 35-day minimum
// between service of a motion and its hearing (LR7.1(a)), an earliest
// date rather than a deadline, which the language does not encode; hard
// copy service on the day of filing (LR5.5); the scheduling order within
// the earlier of 90 days after service or 60 days after appearance
// (LR16.2(a)), which restates FRCP 16(b)(2) and binds the court; the
// Rule 26(f) conference "within twenty-one (21) days before any
// scheduling conference" (LR26.1(a)), which can be read as a window or as
// FRCP 26(f)(1)'s "at least 21 days before" and so is left to lit/frcp;
// the three days LR81.1(e) adds to a response period in a case with a
// self-represented litigant, a FRCP 6(d)-style addition and not a period
// of its own; the receiver's reports every three months after the first
// (LR66.1(b)), a recurring period; the one-year unsealing of criminal
// warrants and the clerk's 60-day notice (LR79.2), criminal and clerk
// duties; and the briefing of bankruptcy appeals, which LR8009.1(a)
// leaves to FRBP 8018(a) (lit/frbp). No fee is stated: the admission and
// pro hac vice fees are "the applicable fee" (LR83.1(b), (c)(2)(C)).
// The earlier D. Haw. outline's FRCP flow and its Supreme Court decisions
// (Twombly, Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Reeves, Catlin,
// Bowles, Hamer) are FRCP and FRAP authority and belong to lit/frcp and
// lit/frap; its Ninth Circuit decisions (Eitel v. McCool; Lopez v. Smith)
// are removed: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A brief or memorandum supporting or opposing any motion, petition or
/// appeal, including a pro se party's: at most 25 pages, or longer if it
/// contains no more than 6,250 words and carries the word-count certificate
/// (LR7.4(a), (b), (e)). Headings, footnotes and quotations count; the
/// caption, tables, exhibits, declarations and certificates do not
/// (LR7.4(d)). The same limits apply to bankruptcy appeals (LR8009.1(c)).
limit memorandum {
  words <= 6_250 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.4(b)"
  pages <= 25 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.4(a)"
} cite "D. Haw. LR 7.4(a)"

/// A reply brief or memorandum: at most 15 pages, unless it contains no
/// more than 3,750 words and carries the word-count certificate (LR7.4(c),
/// (e)).
limit reply-memorandum {
  words <= 3_750 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.4(c)"
  pages <= 15 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.4(c)"
} cite "D. Haw. LR 7.4(c)"

/// A concise statement supporting or opposing a motion for summary
/// judgment: at most 5 pages, unless it contains no more than 1,500 words,
/// counted under LR7.4(d) and certified under LR7.4(e) (LR56.1(c)).
limit concise-statement {
  words <= 1_500 cite "D. Haw. LR 56.1(c)"
  pages <= 5 cite "D. Haw. LR 56.1(c)"
} cite "D. Haw. LR 56.1(c)"

/// A letter brief under the expedited discovery procedure: five pages or
/// less, inclusive of all exhibits, unless the court orders otherwise
/// (LR37.1(c)(2)).
limit discovery-letter-brief { pages <= 5 cite "D. Haw. LR 37.1(c)" } cite "D. Haw. LR 37.1(c)"

/// A motion to file under seal is filed (LR5.2(c)).
event SealMotionFiled()
/// The court denies a motion to file under seal (LR5.2(c)).
event SealMotionDenied()
/// The court enters an order on a motion to file under seal (LR5.2(c)).
event SealOrderEntered()
/// A motion to file publicly a matter another party designated confidential
/// is filed (LR5.2(d)).
event PublicFilingMotionFiled()
/// A document required or permitted to be served is served (LR5.6).
event DocumentServed()
/// The hearing on a motion set for hearing is held (LR7.2, LR7.7).
event MotionHearingHeld()
/// A non-hearing motion is served (LR7.2).
event NonHearingMotionServed() paper memorandum
/// An opposition to a non-hearing motion is served (LR7.2).
event NonHearingOppositionServed() paper memorandum
/// An opposition to a non-hearing counter motion is served (LR7.7).
event CounterMotionOppositionServed() paper reply-memorandum
/// The motion or opposition in which a party seeks to join substantively is
/// filed (LR7.7).
event JoinedPaperFiled()
/// A motion subject to the pre-filing conference is filed (LR7.8).
event MotionFiled() paper memorandum
/// The order granting leave to amend a pleading is filed (LR10.4).
event AmendmentGranted()
/// The scheduling conference is held (LR16.2(b)).
event SchedulingConferenceHeld()
/// The settlement conference is held (LR16.5(b)(1)).
event SettlementConferenceHeld()
/// The FRCP 26(f) conference of the parties is held (LR26.1(b)).
event PartiesConferenceHeld()
/// The plaintiff files the FRCP 26(f) report (LR26.1(b)).
event PlaintiffReportFiled()
/// A Notice of Related Case is served (LR40.2).
event RelatedCaseNoticeServed()
/// Trial begins on the date set (LR47.2, LR51.1).
event TrialBegins()
/// An action tried without a jury, or with an advisory jury under FRCP
/// 39(c), concludes (LR52.1).
event BenchTrialConcluded()
/// Judgment, or the settlement agreement on which a fee motion is founded,
/// is entered (LR54.1(b), LR54.2).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// An order denying a motion under FRCP 50(b), 52(b) or 59 is entered
/// (LR54.1(b)).
event PostTrialMotionDenied()
/// An order remanding a removed action to state court is entered
/// (LR54.1(b)).
event RemandOrderEntered()
/// A Bill of Costs is served (LR54.1(d)).
event BillOfCostsServed()
/// The clerk taxes costs (LR54.1(e)).
event CostsTaxed()
/// The respondent receives the movant's fee records, rates and expense
/// evidence (LR54.2(d)(5)).
event FeeInformationReceived()
/// The LR54.2(d) exchange of fee information is completed (LR54.2(d)).
event FeeExchangeCompleted()
/// A Fee Motion is served (LR54.2(g)).
event FeeMotionServed() paper memorandum
/// The responsive memorandum on a Fee Motion is served (LR54.2(g)).
event FeeResponseServed() paper memorandum
/// The court announces a decision awarding a judgment or order that
/// requires settlement and approval as to form (LR58.2).
event DecisionAnnounced()
/// The prevailing party's draft order or judgment is served (LR58.2).
event DraftJudgmentServed()
/// An interlocutory order is issued (LR60.1).
event InterlocutoryOrderIssued()
/// A receiver or similar officer takes possession of the estate
/// (LR66.1(a)).
event ReceiverTookPossession()
/// The receiver files the inventory (LR66.1(b)).
event ReceiverInventoryFiled()
/// A magistrate judge's non-dispositive order or findings and
/// recommendations is served (LR74.1(a)).
event MagistrateOrderServed()
/// An objection to a magistrate judge's order or findings and
/// recommendations is served (LR74.1(b)).
event MagistrateObjectionServed()
/// The clerk notifies a self-represented litigant that a document or item
/// cannot be scanned and must be served by other means (LR81.1(c)(3)(B)).
event ServiceByOtherMeansNotified()
/// A change occurs that might render an attorney ineligible to practice in
/// the court (LR83.1(d)).
event AttorneyStatusChanged()
/// An attorney's or self-represented litigant's address or contact
/// information changes (LR83.1(e)(1)).
event ContactInformationChanged()
/// A document the court directed to an attorney or self-represented
/// litigant is returned as not deliverable (LR83.1(e)(2)).
event CourtMailReturned()
/// The court mails a notice to show cause why disbarment or suspension
/// should not occur (LR83.4(b)).
event DisciplineNoticeMailed()
/// A party learns the identity of a mediator the court selected, or facts
/// that form the basis of an objection (LR88.1(l)).
event MediatorIdentityLearned()
/// A motion to vacate or correct sentence under 28 U.S.C. § 2255 is served
/// (LR99.3(d)).
event Section2255MotionServed()
/// The scheduling order in a pro se prisoner action is entered (LR99.16.2).
event PrisonerSchedulingOrderEntered()
/// The bankruptcy court enters an order under LR8005.1(a) dismissing an
/// appeal or ruling on an extension or consolidation (LR8005.1(b)).
event BankruptcyAppealOrderEntered()

/// LR5.2(c): no later than 7 days after the filing of a motion to seal, any
/// person may oppose it.
deadline seal-opposition-period: 7.days after SealMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 5.2(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR5.2(c): if the court denies the motion, the movant informs the court
/// within 4 days whether it wants to withdraw the document or have it filed
/// publicly; absent notice within 4 days the document is returned to the
/// movant.
deadline seal-denial-election-period: 4.days after SealMotionDenied() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 5.2(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR5.2(c): the movant, within 4 days of an order, files a version of the
/// document consistent with the order.
deadline seal-conforming-filing-period: 4.days after SealOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 5.2(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR5.2(d): within 7 days after a motion to file publicly a matter another
/// party designated confidential is filed, any party may oppose it and seek
/// to have the matter sealed.
deadline public-filing-opposition-period: 7.days after PublicFilingMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 5.2(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR5.6: proof of service is filed or mailed for filing within 1 day of
/// service, except where the FRCP prescribes a particular method of proof.
deadline proof-of-service-period: 1.days after DocumentServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 5.6"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR7.2: an opposition to a motion set for hearing, or a statement of no
/// opposition or no position, is served and filed at least 21 days before
/// the hearing. Summary judgment briefing follows the same schedule
/// (LR56.1(a), (j)).
deadline hearing-opposition-period: 21.days before MotionHearingHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR7.2: an opposition to a non-hearing motion, or a statement of no
/// opposition or no position, is served and filed within 14 days after
/// service of the motion.
deadline nonhearing-opposition-period: 14.days after NonHearingMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR7.2: any reply in support of a motion set for hearing is served and
/// filed at least 14 days before the hearing. An untimely opposition or
/// reply may be disregarded or stricken.
deadline hearing-reply-period: 14.days before MotionHearingHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR7.2: any reply in support of a non-hearing motion is served and filed
/// within 14 days after service of the opposition.
deadline nonhearing-reply-period: 14.days after NonHearingOppositionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR7.7: the movant on a counter motion set for hearing files and serves
/// any reply at least 7 days before the hearing.
deadline counter-motion-hearing-reply-period: 7.days before MotionHearingHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.7"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR7.7: the movant on a non-hearing counter motion files and serves any
/// reply within 7 days after service of the opposition to the counter
/// motion.
deadline counter-motion-nonhearing-reply-period: 7.days after CounterMotionOppositionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.7"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR7.7: except with leave of court for good cause, a substantive joinder
/// in a motion or opposition is filed and served within 3 days of the
/// filing of the motion or opposition joined in. A joinder of simple
/// agreement may be filed at any time.
deadline substantive-joinder-period: 3.days after JoinedPaperFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.7"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR7.8: counsel contemplating a motion confer with opposing counsel at
/// least 7 days before filing it; discovery motions (LR37.1), TRO and
/// preliminary injunction applications, matters with a pro se party, and
/// motions during trial are excepted.
deadline prefiling-conference-period: 7.days before MotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 7.8"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR10.4: if leave is granted, the amended pleading is filed, with redline
/// formatting removed, and served within 14 days of the filing of the order
/// granting leave, unless the court orders otherwise.
deadline amended-pleading-period: 14.days after AmendmentGranted() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 10.4"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR16.2(b): each party files and serves a Scheduling Conference Statement
/// at least 7 days before the scheduling conference.
deadline scheduling-statement-period: 7.days before SchedulingConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 16.2(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR16.5(b)(1): at least 7 days before the settlement conference, each
/// party delivers a Confidential Settlement Conference Statement directly
/// to the settlement judge; it is not filed or served.
deadline settlement-statement-period: 7.days before SettlementConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 16.5(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR26.1(b): unless the parties agree or the court orders otherwise, the
/// plaintiff files the FRCP 26(f) report within 14 days after the
/// conference.
deadline parties-report-period: 14.days after PartiesConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 26.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR26.1(b): the defendant may file a supplemental report within 7 days if
/// it objects to the plaintiff's report. The rule names no trigger; the
/// period is read to run from the plaintiff's report to which it objects.
deadline supplemental-report-period: 7.days after PlaintiffReportFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 26.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR40.2: a party receiving a Notice of Related Case responds within 7
/// days of service, or its objections are waived.
deadline related-case-response-period: 7.days after RelatedCaseNoticeServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 40.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR47.2: when a civil case set for jury trial settles or is otherwise
/// disposed of, counsel notify the court at least one full business day
/// before trial is set to begin, or juror costs may be assessed.
deadline jury-settlement-notice-period: 1.court_days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 47.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR51.1(e): unless otherwise ordered, the parties serve their proposed
/// jury instructions on each other at least 21 days before trial, then meet
/// and confer.
deadline jury-instruction-exchange-period: 21.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 51.1(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR51.1(g): the jointly agreed and separately proposed instructions are
/// filed at least 14 days before trial.
deadline jury-instruction-filing-period: 14.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 51.1(g)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR51.1(g): each party files its written objections to the instructions
/// the other party proposed at least 7 days before trial.
deadline jury-instruction-objection-period: 7.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 51.1(g)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR52.1: except as otherwise ordered, within 28 days of the conclusion of
/// an action tried without a jury the parties simultaneously file separate
/// draft findings of fact and conclusions of law.
deadline draft-findings-period: 28.days after BenchTrialConcluded() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 52.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.1(b): unless otherwise ordered, a Bill of Costs is filed and served
/// within 14 days after entry of judgment. Non-compliance with LR54.1 is
/// deemed a waiver of costs (LR54.1(a)).
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.1(b): a Bill of Costs is filed and served within 14 days after
/// entry of an order denying a motion under FRCP 50(b), 52(b) or 59.
deadline post-trial-bill-of-costs-period: 14.days after PostTrialMotionDenied() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.1(b): a Bill of Costs is filed and served within 14 days after
/// entry of an order remanding a removed action to state court.
deadline remand-bill-of-costs-period: 14.days after RemandOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.1(d): within 7 days after a Bill of Costs is served, the party
/// against whom costs are claimed files and serves any specific objections;
/// absent objections the clerk may tax all the requested costs.
deadline costs-objection-period: 7.days after BillOfCostsServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.1(e): taxation of costs may be reviewed by the court on motion
/// filed and served within 7 days after taxation by the clerk, under FRCP
/// 54(d)(1).
deadline costs-review-motion-period: 7.days after CostsTaxed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.1(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.2(b): unless a court order sets a different schedule, a Fee Motion
/// is filed and served within 49 days after entry of the judgment or
/// settlement agreement on which it is founded. FRCP 54(d)(2)(B) yields its
/// 14 days to a "statute or a court order"; whether a local rule is such an
/// order is not settled by the vendored text, so this period stands beside
/// lit/frcp's, not over it.
deadline fee-motion-period: 49.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.2(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.2(d)(4): the movant provides the respondent its time records, rates
/// and expense evidence within 14 days after the judgment, unless the court
/// sets a different schedule.
deadline fee-information-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.2(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.2(d)(5): if no agreement is reached, the respondent, within 14 days
/// of receipt of that information, discloses the evidence it will use to
/// oppose the requested hours, rates or expenses.
deadline fee-disclosure-period: 14.days after FeeInformationReceived() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.2(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.2(d): 7 days after the exchange of information is completed and
/// before the motion is filed, the parties identify the hours, rates and
/// expenses that will and will not be objected to.
deadline fee-objection-identification-period: 7.days after FeeExchangeCompleted() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.2(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.2(e): the parties complete the joint statement within 42 days after
/// entry of the judgment or settlement agreement on which the fee motion
/// will be based, unless the court orders otherwise.
deadline fee-joint-statement-period: 42.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.2(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.2(g): unless otherwise ordered, any opposing party may file and
/// serve a responsive memorandum within 7 days after service of the Fee
/// Motion.
deadline fee-response-period: 7.days after FeeMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.2(g)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR54.2(g): the movant may file and serve a reply memorandum within 7
/// days after service of the responsive memorandum; the motion is then
/// decided without a hearing unless otherwise ordered.
deadline fee-reply-period: 7.days after FeeResponseServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 54.2(g)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR58.2: except as otherwise ordered, within 7 days after the
/// announcement of a decision awarding a judgment or order that requires
/// settlement and approval as to form, the prevailing party files and
/// serves a draft.
deadline draft-judgment-period: 7.days after DecisionAnnounced() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 58.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR58.2: a party receiving the proposed draft files and serves, within 7
/// days, any objection and a substitute proposed draft.
deadline draft-judgment-objection-period: 7.days after DraftJudgmentServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 58.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR60.1: a motion for reconsideration of an interlocutory order for
/// manifest error of law or fact (LR60.1(c)) is filed and served within 14
/// days after the order is issued. Reconsideration of a case-dispositive
/// order is governed by FRCP 59 or 60 (lit/frcp).
deadline reconsideration-period: 14.days after InterlocutoryOrderIssued() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 60.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR66.1(a): unless otherwise ordered, a receiver or similar officer files
/// an inventory within 28 days after taking possession of the estate.
deadline receiver-inventory-period: 28.days after ReceiverTookPossession() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 66.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR66.1(b): within one month after the filing of the inventory, unless
/// the court directs other times, the receiver files a report of receipts,
/// expenditures and transactions; later reports follow at three-month
/// intervals (not encoded, a recurring period).
deadline receiver-first-report-period: 1.months after ReceiverInventoryFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 66.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR74.1(a): except where the parties consented under LR73.1, a party may
/// object to a magistrate judge's non-dispositive order or findings and
/// recommendations within 14 days after being served. A reconsideration
/// motion tolls the time (LR74.1(d)).
deadline magistrate-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateOrderServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 74.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR74.1(b): any party may file and serve a response within 14 days after
/// service of the objection; no reply without leave (LR74.1(c)).
deadline magistrate-objection-response-period: 14.days after MagistrateObjectionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 74.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR81.1(c)(3)(B): when a self-represented litigant presents a document or
/// item that cannot be scanned, the clerk notifies the litigant to serve it
/// by other means within 3 business days.
deadline pro-se-other-service-period: 3.court_days after ServiceByOtherMeansNotified() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 81.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR83.1(d): an attorney who is a member of the bar of the court, or has
/// permission to practice in it, files notice of a change that might render
/// the attorney ineligible within 14 days of the change.
deadline attorney-status-notice-period: 14.days after AttorneyStatusChanged() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 83.1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR83.1(e)(1): an attorney or self-represented litigant whose address or
/// contact information changes while appearing in a pending case files and
/// serves a Notice of Change of Address within 14 days.
deadline address-change-notice-period: 14.days after ContactInformationChanged() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 83.1(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR83.1(e)(2): sanctions, including dismissal or judgment, may follow
/// when a document the court directed to an attorney or self-represented
/// litigant is returned as not deliverable and the court receives no
/// written current address within 30 days of the return.
deadline returned-mail-response-period: 30.days after CourtMailReturned() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 83.1(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR83.4(b): a person disbarred or suspended elsewhere, found guilty of a
/// qualifying crime, or no longer meeting the admission requirements shows
/// cause within 14 days after the mailing of the notice why disbarment or
/// suspension in this court should not occur.
deadline discipline-show-cause-period: 14.days after DisciplineNoticeMailed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 83.4(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR88.1(l): a party objecting to a mediator the court selected files an
/// objection within 7 days after learning the mediator's identity, or
/// within 7 days of learning the facts on which the objection rests.
deadline mediator-objection-period: 7.days after MediatorIdentityLearned() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 88.1(l)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR99.3(d): within 35 days of service of a motion to vacate or correct
/// sentence under 28 U.S.C. § 2255, the respondent files a response, unless
/// otherwise ordered.
deadline section-2255-response-period: 35.days after Section2255MotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 99.3(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR99.16.2: in a pro se prisoner action, a motion asserting failure to
/// exhaust prison administrative remedies under 42 U.S.C. § 1997e(a) is
/// filed within 70 days after entry of the scheduling order.
deadline prisoner-exhaustion-motion-period: 70.days after PrisonerSchedulingOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 99.16.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR8005.1(b): a bankruptcy court order under LR8005.1(a) may be reviewed
/// by the district court on motion filed within 14 days after entry of the
/// order.
deadline bankruptcy-appeal-order-review-period: 14.days after BankruptcyAppealOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Haw. LR 8005.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}
